.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH terminal-of-tinsel-completions 1  "completions " 
.SH NAME
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-completions \- Print a shell completion script
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBterminal\-of\-tinsel completions\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-pack\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISHELL\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the script that teaches your shell to complete terminal\-of\-tinsel: commands, flags, creature names and pack ids, community packs included. The script asks the program itself what to offer, so it never goes out of date.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the command\*(Aqs data as JSON instead of drawing it (errors become a JSON object on stderr)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Plain output: no colour, no emoji, ASCII borders (also set by NO_COLOR, or by piping)
.TP
\fB\-\-pack\fR \fI<PACK>\fR
Only use creatures from these packs, e.g. \-\-pack nordic,dickens
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fISHELL\fR>
The shell to complete for
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
bash
.IP \(bu 2
elvish
.IP \(bu 2
fish
.IP \(bu 2
powershell
.IP \(bu 2
zsh
.RE
.SH EXTRA
For example, in ~/.zshrc:
  source <(terminal\-of\-tinsel completions zsh)

Then:
  terminal\-of\-tinsel creature kra<TAB>
